kunzite: Adreno 710, glue plan K1 (main repo ios/gpu-glue-plan.md 4): keep mode. With kgpu_keep=1
(and kgpu >= 21; kgpu=22 runs steps 1..21) the run is not undone after step 21: OOB_GPU stays set
(GX on), HFI stays up, the CP runs out of secure mode, idle, and redwood_gpu_ready() is true
(redwood_gpu_on() too, from the boot-args). At once and every kgpu_keep_report seconds (default 60,
0 = never), two lines: GX GDSC, the GMU's RPMh power state, GFX power/clock status and CX busy,
RBBM_STATUS, CP RPTR/WPTR, SQE_CNTL, HW_FAULT, CB0 FSR, GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO and the HFI message and
debug queue indices; then UCHE_GMEM_RANGE_MIN/MAX (0 right after gen7_start on #41/#45/#47: do they
hold once GX is kept?), RBBM_NC_MODE_CNTL (the macrotile mode, glue plan 3.3) and the five hbb-14
registers (0990). Whatever the GMU queued is drained and printed. The GPU goes by the run's own undo
(CP halted first, slumber, GMU into reset, CX off) after kgpu_keep_s seconds (default 0 = never), or
at shutdown: reboot_kernel (bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c) calls kunzite_adreno_shutdown(howto) before
processes are told to exit, unless it is a panic; that wakes the probe's thread, which undoes
everything itself, and waits at most 5 s. A shutdown during a run also stops it between steps and
undoes it. Test: kgpu=21 kgpu_keep=1 kgpu_keep_s=1800: 30 min kept with a report a minute, agent and
UI as usual, then the undo as on #47.

